/Author (Hunter Hughes)
/CreationDate (D\07220261117144506\05505\04700\047)
/Creator (H Heuristics PDF pipeline)
/Keywords (polycrisis resilience\054 systemic risk\054 vulnerability reduction\054 climate\054 pollution\054 poverty\054 conflict\054 demographic shift\054 human exposure\054 adaptation\054 long\055horizon\054 development pathways)
/ModDate (D\07220261117144506\05505\04700\047)
/Producer (ReportLab PDF Library \055 www\056reportlab\056com)
/Subject (Humanity\047s largest risks now reinforce one another\072 heat cuts harvests\054 prices rise\054 thin budgets cannot absorb the shock\054 and weakened institutions adapt less\056 This report defines Polycrisis Resilience as the capacity of human populations\054 societies\054 economies\054 institutions and interconnected ecological systems to anticipate\054 withstand\054 adapt to and recover from multiple interacting crises\054 while systematically reducing the underlying vulnerabilities that amplify their consequences\056 It argues that the concept is not another word for general robustness but an integrated\054 long\055horizon approach whose measure of success is lower vulnerability\054 not faster recovery\056 The concept and framework are presented as developed by Hunter Hughes\054 Founder of H Heuristics\054 and the report builds on two H Heuristics essays published in March 2025\056)
/Title (Polycrisis Resilience\072 Flagship Report\072 Defining the Concept\054 Understanding the Global Polycrisis\054 and Establishing the H Heuristics Framework)
/Trapped /False
>>
